{"results":[{"url":"https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/67511701/united-states-v-biden/","final_url":"https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/67511701/united-states-v-biden/","title":"United States v. Biden, 1:23-cr-00061 - CourtListener.com","description":"Docket for United States v. Biden, 1:23-cr-00061 — Brought to you by Free Law Project, a non-profit dedicated to creating high quality open legal information.","language":"en","text":"Items on this page are sourced from PACER and RECAP and may not be up to date. Learn more about our coverage.\n\n1\n\nJun 20, 2023\n\nLetter to Deputy Clerk from United States Attorney's Office for the District of Delaware regarding filing of Informations. (kjk) (Entered: 06/20/2023)\n\nLetter\n\n2\n\nJun 20, 2023\n\nFELONY INFORMATION as to Robert Hunter Biden (1) count 1. (Attachments: # 1 Defendant Information Sheet) (kjk) (Entered: 06/20/2023)\n\nInformation - Felony\n\nDefendant Information Sheet\n\nJun 21, 2023\n\nCase assigned to Judge Maryellen Noreika, as to Robert Hunter Biden. Please include the initials of the Judge (MN) after the case number on all documents filed. (rjb)\n\nCase Assigned/Reassigned\n\n3\n\nJun 21, 2023\n\nORDER SCHEDULING HEARING as to Robert Hunter Biden: An Initial Appearance is set for 7/26/2023 at 10:00 AM in Courtroom 4A before Judge Maryellen Noreika. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 6/21/2023. (as) (Entered: 06/21/2023)\n\nOrder\n\n4\n\nJun 26, 2023\n\nSummons Returned Executed on 6/23/23 as to Robert Hunter Biden (SEALED) (kjk) (Entered: 06/26/2023)\n\nMain Doc\n\nSummons Returned Executed\n\n5\n\nJul 7, 2023\n\nNOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Richard I.G. Jones, Jr appearing for Robert Hunter Biden (Jones, Richard) (Entered: 07/07/2023)\n\nNotice of Attorney Appearance - Defendant\n\n6\n\nJul 10, 2023\n\nCertificate of Good Standing as to Attorney Christopher J. Clark. (as) (Entered: 07/10/2023)\n\nCertificate of Good Standing\n\n7\n\nJul 20, 2023\n\nNOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Matthew S. Salerno appearing for Robert Hunter Biden. (as) (Entered: 07/20/2023)\n\nNotice of Attorney Appearance - Defendant\n\n8\n\nJul 20, 2023\n\nCertificate of Good Standing as to Attorney Matthew S. Salerno. (as) (Entered: 07/20/2023)\n\nCertificate of Good Standing\n\n9\n\nJul 20, 2023\n\nNOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Attorney Brian C. McManus appearing for Robert Hunter Biden. (as) (Entered: 07/20/2023)\n\nNotice of Attorney Appearance - Defendant\n\n10\n\nJul 20, 2023\n\nCertificate of Good Standing as to Attorney Brian C. McManus. (as) (Entered: 07/20/2023)\n\nCertificate of Good Standing\n\n11\n\nJul 20, 2023\n\nNOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Timothy H. McCarten appearing for Robert Hunter Biden. (as) (Entered: 07/20/2023)\n\nNotice of Attorney Appearance - Defendant\n\n12\n\nJul 20, 2023\n\nCertificate of Good Standing as to Attorney Timothy H. McCarten. (as) (Entered: 07/20/2023)\n\nCertificate of Good Standing\n\n13\n\nJul 25, 2023\n\nLetter to The Honorable Maryellen Noreika from Julianne E. Murray regarding Motion for Leave to File Amicus Brief with Accompanying Amicus Brief. (Attachments: # 1 Motion for Leave to File Amicus Brief, # 2 Amicus Brief with Mike Howell Declaration, # 3 Amicus Brief Exhibits 1-12, # 4 Amicus Brief Exhibits 13-23)(Murray, Julianne) (Entered: 07/25/2023)\n\nLetter\n\nMotion for Leave to File Amicus Brief\n\nAmicus Brief with Mike Howell Declaration\n\nAmicus Brief Exhibits 1-12\n\nAmicus Brief Exhibits 13-23\n\nJul 26, 2023\n\nMinute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Maryellen Noreika - Initial Appearance as to Robert Hunter Biden on (1) Count 1 held on 7/26/2023., Defendant was present with counsel. The Court advised Defendant of rights and granted release with conditions. Defendant waived the preliminary hearing. The Court advised counsel of their Brady obligations under Rule 5(f). The Court deferred a decision on the plea and pretrial diversion agreement. The parties shall submit briefs as ordered within 30 days; Not Guilty Plea entered. Time is excluded from the Speedy Trial Act between today and 9/1/2023 in the interests of justice. Appearances: B. Wallace, Esq., L. Wise, Esq., & D. Hines, Esq. for USA; C. Clark, Esq. & R. Jones, Esq. for DEFT; M. Bray & B. Williams for USPO; M. Buckson DEPUTY; (Court Reporter Dale Hawkins.) (mdb)\n\nInitial Appearance\n\n14\n\nJul 26, 2023\n\nORDER pursuant to Fed. R. Crim. P. 5(f) as to Robert Hunter Biden. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 7/26/2023. (mdb) (Entered: 07/26/2023)\n\nORDER pursuant to Fed. R. Crim. P. 5(f)\n\n15\n\nJul 26, 2023\n\nORDER Setting Conditions of Release as to Robert Hunter Biden (1) O/R with conditions. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 7/26/2023. (mdb) (Entered: 07/26/2023)\n\nOrder Setting Conditions of Release\n\n16\n\nJul 27, 2023\n\nOFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT of Initial Appearance held on 07/26/2023 before Judge Maryellen Noreika. Court Reporter: Dale C. Hawkins,Email: Dale\\_Hawkins@ded.uscourts.gov. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or order/purchased through the Court Reporter before the deadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date, it may be obtained through PACER. Redaction Request due 8/17/2023. Redacted Transcript Deadline set for 8/28/2023. Release of Transcript Restriction set for 10/25/2023. (dh) (Entered: 07/27/2023)\n\nTranscript\n\n17\n\nJul 28, 2023\n\nORDER - IT IS HEREBY ORDERED that, going forward, any issues or inquiries in the above-captioned cases shall be brought to my attention and not to the Clerk's Office. Any such issues and inquiries shall be submitted in writing and placed on the docket. To the extent that the rare instance arises in which a writing is not practicable, a phone call may be made to my Chambers by an attorney who represents one of the parties in these cases or an interested third party. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 7/28/2023. (dlw) (Entered: 07/28/2023)\n\nOrder\n\n18\n\nJul 28, 2023\n\nORAL ORDER: The Court has received the attached request. On or before close of business on August 1, 2023, the parties shall provide their respective positions on the request to docket the proposed agreements. ORDERED by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 7/28/2023. (mdb) (Entered: 07/28/2023)\n\nOrder\n\n19\n\nAug 1, 2023\n\nMOTION for Authorization to File Electronically Using the CM/ECF System filed PRO SE by Christopher J. Tigani. (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit A - Pacer Invoice, # 2 Exhibit B - Certificate of Service Email)(as) (Entered: 08/01/2023)\n\nMotion for Leave to File\n\nExhibit A - Pacer Invoice\n\nExhibit B - Certificate of Service Email\n\n20\n\nAug 1, 2023\n\nLetter to The Honorable Maryellen Noreika from Benjamin L. Wallace, Assistant United States Attorney regarding Response to NBC News Request - re 18 Order,. (Wallace, Benjamin) (Entered: 08/01/2023)\n\nLetter\n\n21\n\nAug 1, 2023\n\nLetter to The Honorable Maryellen Noreika from Christopher J. Clark, Esq. regarding Defendant's position on the request to docket the Memorandum of Plea Agreement and Diversion Agreement. - re 18 Order,. (Jones, Richard) (Entered: 08/01/2023)\n\nLetter\n\n22\n\nAug 2, 2023\n\nORAL ORDER: On July 28, 2023, the Court received a letter from a reporter at NBC News requesting that the agreements discussed at the July 26, 2023 hearing be docketed. [D.I. 18 in Cr. A. No. 23-61; D.I. 21 in Cr. A. No. 23-274]. The parties do not object to the request. [D.I. 20, 21 in Cr. A. No. 23-61; D.I. 24, 25 in Cr. A. No. 23-274]. THEREFORE IT IS HEREBY ORDERED that the request is GRANTED. Additionally, at the July 26, 2023 hearing, the parties provided the Court with the Memorandum of Plea Agreement, but did not provide the Court with the Pretrial Diversion Agreement. The Court will docket the signed Memorandum of Plea Agreement and IT IS HEREBY FURTHER ORDERED that the parties shall docket the Pretrial Diversion Agreement discussed at the hearing by NOON today. ORDERED by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 8/2/2023. (mdb) (Entered: 08/02/2023)\n\nMain Doc\n\nOral Order\n\n23\n\nAug 2, 2023\n\nLetter to The Honorable Maryellen Noreika from Julianne E. Murray regarding Motion for Leave to Intervene and Memorandum in Opposition of Defendants Motion for Leave to File Under Seal. (Attachments: # 1 Motion for Leave to Intervene, # 2 Declaration of Julianne E. Murray with Exhibits, # 3 Proposed Order, # 4 Memorandum of Opposition to Defendants Motion for Leave to File Under Seal)(Murray, Julianne) (Entered: 08/02/2023)\n\nLetter\n\nMotion for Leave to Intervene\n\nDeclaration of Julianne E. Murray with Exhibits\n\nProposed Order\n\nMemorandum of Opposition to Defendants Motion for Leave to File Under Seal\n\n24\n\nAug 2, 2023\n\nLetter to The Honorable Maryellen Noreika from Christopher J. Clark, Esq. regarding Filing the Executed copy of the Diversion Agreement - re 22 Oral Order,,,. (Attachments: # 1 Diversion Agreement)(Jones, Richard) (Entered: 08/02/2023)\n\nLetter\n\nDiversion Agreement\n\n25\n\nAug 11, 2023\n\nMOTION to Vacate the Court's Briefing Order by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Hines, Derek). (Entered: 08/11/2023)\n\nMotion to Vacate\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n26\n\nAug 11, 2023\n\nORAL ORDER - IT IS HEREBY ORDERED that, by no later that NOON on Monday, August 14, 2023, Defendant shall file a response to the United States' 25 Motion to Vacate the Court's Briefing Order. ORDERED by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 8/11/2023. (dlw) (Entered: 08/11/2023)\n\nMain Doc\n\nOral Order\n\n27\n\nAug 13, 2023\n\nRESPONSE to Motion by Robert Hunter Biden re 25 MOTION to Vacate the Court's Briefing Order (Jones, Richard). (Entered: 08/13/2023)\n\nResponse to Motion\n\n28\n\nAug 14, 2023\n\nNOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Abbe David Lowell, Esq. appearing for Robert Hunter Biden. (as) (Entered: 08/14/2023)\n\nNotice of Attorney Appearance - Defendant\n\n29\n\nAug 14, 2023\n\nCertificate of Good Standing as to Attorney Abbe David Lowell. (as) (Entered: 08/14/2023)\n\nCertificate of Good Standing\n\n30\n\nAug 14, 2023\n\nORAL ORDER - IT IS HEREBY ORDERED that, by no later than NOON on Tuesday, August 15, 2023, the Government shall file a reply to Defendant's 27 Response. ORDERED by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 8/14/2023. (dlw) (Entered: 08/14/2023)\n\nMain Doc\n\nOral Order\n\n31\n\nAug 15, 2023\n\nMOTION for Christopher J. Clark to Withdraw as Attorney by Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Jones, Richard) (Entered: 08/15/2023)\n\nMotion to Withdraw as Attorney\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n32\n\nAug 15, 2023\n\nREPLY TO RESPONSE to Motion to Vacate the Court's Briefing Order ( 25 ) by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden (Hines, Derek). (Entered: 08/15/2023)\n\nReply to Response\n\n33\n\nAug 16, 2023\n\nRESPONSE to Motion by Robert Hunter Biden re 31 MOTION for Christopher J. Clark to Withdraw as Attorney (Jones, Richard). (Entered: 08/16/2023)\n\nResponse to Motion\n\n34\n\nAug 17, 2023\n\nORDER granting 25 Motion to Vacate the Court's briefing order of July 26, 2023 as to Robert Hunter Biden. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 8/17/2023. (as) (Entered: 08/17/2023)\n\nOrder on Motion to Vacate\n\nAug 17, 2023\n\nORAL ORDER as to Robert Hunter Biden GRANTING 31 MOTION for Christopher J. Clark to Withdraw as Attorney . Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 8/17/2023. (as)\n\nOral Order\n\n35\n\nAug 18, 2023\n\nMOTION for Brian C. McManus, Matthew S. Salerno, and Timothy H. McCarten of Latham & Watkins LLP to Withdraw as Attorney by Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Jones, Richard) (Entered: 08/18/2023)\n\nMotion to Withdraw as Attorney\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\nAug 21, 2023\n\nSO ORDERED re 35 MOTION for Brian C. McManus, Matthew S. Salerno, and Timothy H. McCarten of Latham & Watkins LLP to Withdraw as Attorney filed by Robert Hunter Biden. Attorney Matthew S. Salerno; Timothy H. McCarten and Brian C. McManus terminated in case as to Robert Hunter Biden. ORDERED by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 8/21/2023. (mdb)\n\nOral Order\n\n36\n\nAug 31, 2023\n\nORAL ORDER: In view of the Speedy Trial Act, IT IS HEREBY ORDERED that, on or before Wednesday, September 6, 2023, the parties are directed to provide the Court with an update on the status of this case, including any steps that they believe the Court needs to take. ORDERED by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 8/31/2023. (mdb) (Entered: 08/31/2023)\n\nMain Doc\n\nOral Order\n\n37\n\nSep 6, 2023\n\nSTATUS REPORT by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden (Wise, Leo) (Entered: 09/06/2023)\n\nStatus Report\n\n38\n\nSep 6, 2023\n\nSTATUS REPORT by Robert Hunter Biden (Jones, Richard) (Entered: 09/06/2023)\n\nStatus Report\n\n39\n\nSep 14, 2023\n\nINDICTMENT as to Robert Hunter Biden (1) count(s) 1s, 2, 3. ( Original SEALED - to be maintained in the Clerk's Office ). (kjk) (Entered: 09/14/2023)\n\nIndictment\n\n40\n\nSep 14, 2023\n\nREDACTED VERSION of 39 Indictment by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden (Attachments: # 1 Defendant Information Sheet)(kjk) (Entered: 09/14/2023)\n\nRedacted Document\n\nDefendant Information Sheet\n\n41\n\nSep 18, 2023\n\nORAL ORDER: The Court, understanding that Defendant seeks to have the initial appearance on the Indictment in this matter held via video conference, and understanding that the Government opposes that request, hereby ORDERS as follows: (1) By no later than September 19, 2023, Defendant shall make any such request to the Court in writing by filing a one-page motion to that effect, along with an accompanying letter brief not to exceed two single-spaced pages.; and (2) By no later than September 20, 2023, the Government may file an answering letter brief of no more than two single-spaced pages. Ordered by Judge Christopher J. Burke on 9/18/23. (kjk) (Entered: 09/18/2023)\n\nMain Doc\n\nOral Order\n\n42\n\nSep 19, 2023\n\nMOTION for Leave to Appear Defendants Motion for Leave to Attend Initial Appearance by Video Conference re by Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Letter Brief in Support, # 2 Text of Proposed Order)(Jones, Richard) (Entered: 09/19/2023)\n\nMotion to Appear\n\nLetter Brief in Support\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n43\n\nSep 20, 2023\n\nRESPONSE to Motion by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden re 42 MOTION for Leave to Appear Defendants Motion for Leave to Attend Initial Appearance by Video Conference re (Hines, Derek) (Entered: 09/20/2023)\n\nResponse to Motion\n\n44\n\nSep 20, 2023\n\nORDER as to Robert Hunter Biden re 42 DENYING the MOTION for Leave to Attend Initial Appearance by Video Conference filed by Robert Hunter Biden. The Initial Appearance and Arraignment are set for 9/26/2023 at 10:00 AM in Courtroom 2A before Judge Christopher J. Burke. Signed by Judge Christopher J. Burke on 9/20/23. (kjk) (Entered: 09/20/2023)\n\nOrder\n\n45\n\nSep 20, 2023\n\nOral Order: The Court, having considered an unopposed request from Defendants counsel to reschedule the hearing previously set for September 26, 2023 at 10:00 a.m., hereby ORDERS that the Initial Appearance and Arraignment will be continued until October 3, 2023 at 10:00 a.m. in Courtroom 2A. Ordered by Judge Christopher J. Burke on 9/20/23. (kjk) (Entered: 09/20/2023)\n\nMain Doc\n\nOral Order\n\n46\n\nSep 29, 2023\n\nORDER: The Motion for Leave to File Electronically by third-party Christopher J. Tigani ( 19 ) is DENIED without prejudice. \\*Copy mailed to Mr. Tigani at address listed in motion\\*. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 9/29/2023. (mdb) (Entered: 09/29/2023)\n\nOrder on Motion for Leave to File\n\nOct 3, 2023\n\nMinute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Christopher J. Burke - Initial Appearance as to Robert Hunter Biden held on 10/3/2023; Deft. appeared with retained counsel; Deft. ordered released on his Own Recognizance with special conditions. ATTENDEES: AUSA - L. Wise, Esq.; D. Hines, Esq.; DEFT - A. Lowell, Esq.; R. Jones, Esq,; USPO - M. Bray; CLERK - Kincaid. ( Ct. Reporter - D. Hawkins ) (kjk) Modified on 10/3/2023 (kjk).\n\nInitial Appearance\n\nOct 3, 2023\n\nMinute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Christopher J. Burke - Initial Appearance as to Robert Hunter Biden held on 10/3/2023; Deft. appeared with retained counsel; Deft. ordered released on his Own Recognizance with special conditions. ATTENDEES: AUSA - L. Wise, Esq.; D. Hines, Esq.; DEFT - A. Lowell, Esq.; R. Jones, Esq,; USPO - M. Bray; CLERK - Kincaid. (kjk)\n\n47\n\nOct 3, 2023\n\nORDER Setting Conditions of Release as to Robert Hunter Biden (1) Own Recognizance with special conditions. Signed by Judge Christopher J. Burke on 10/3/23. (kjk) (Entered: 10/03/2023)\n\nOrder Setting Conditions of Release\n\nOct 3, 2023\n\nMinute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Christopher J. Burke - Defendant was present with counsel; Defendant waived reading of the Indictment Arraignment as to Robert Hunter Biden (1) Count 1s,2,3 held. Not Guilty Plea Entered. Pretrial Motions due by 11/3/2023. ATTENDEES: AUSA - L. Wise, Esq.; D. Hines, Esq.; DEFT - A. Lowell, Esq.; R. Jones, Esq.; USPO - M. Bray; CLERK - Kincaid. ( Ct. Reporter - D. Hawkins ) (kjk) Modified on 10/3/2023 (kjk).\n\nArraignment\n\nOct 3, 2023\n\nMinute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Christopher J. Burke - Defendant was present with counsel; Defendant waived reading of the Indictment Arraignment as to Robert Hunter Biden (1) Count 1s,2,3 held. Not Guilty Plea Entered. Pretrial Motions due by 11/3/2023. ATTENDEES: AUSA - L. Wise, Esa.; D. Hines, Esq.; DEFT - A. Lowell, Esq.; R. Jones, Esq.; USPO - M. Bray; CLERK - Kincaid. ( Ct. Reporter - D. Hawkins ) (kjk)\n\n48\n\nOct 3, 2023\n\nORDER TO CONTINUE in the Interests of Justice in order to file pretrial motions as to Robert Hunter Biden. Time excluded from 10/3/23 until 11/3/23. Pretrial Motions due by 11/3/2023. Signed by Judge Christopher J. Burke on 11/3/23. (kjk) (Entered: 10/03/2023)\n\nOrder to Continue - Pretrial Motion Filing\n\n49\n\nOct 3, 2023\n\nOFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT of Initial Appearance/Arraignment held on 10/03/2023 before Judge Christopher J. Burke. Court Reporter: Dale C. Hawkins,Email: Dale\\_Hawkins@ded.uscourts.gov. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or order/purchased through the Court Reporter before the deadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date, it may be obtained through PACER. Redaction Request due 10/24/2023. Redacted Transcript Deadline set for 11/3/2023. Release of Transcript Restriction set for 1/2/2024. (dh) (Entered: 10/03/2023)\n\nTranscript\n\n50\n\nOct 4, 2023\n\nNOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Bartholomew J. Dalton appearing for Robert Hunter Biden (Dalton, Bartholomew) (Entered: 10/04/2023)\n\nNotice of Attorney Appearance - Defendant\n\n51\n\nOct 4, 2023\n\nMOTION to Dismiss Firearm Information Because An Indictment Was Returned by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Wise, Leo). (Entered: 10/04/2023)\n\nMotion to Dismiss\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n52\n\nOct 4, 2023\n\nAmended MOTION to Dismiss Firearm Information Because An Indictment Was Returned by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Wise, Leo). (Entered: 10/04/2023)\n\nMotion to Dismiss\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n53\n\nOct 5, 2023\n\nRESPONSE to Motion by Robert Hunter Biden re 52 Amended MOTION to Dismiss Firearm Information Because An Indictment Was Returned, 51 MOTION to Dismiss Firearm Information Because An Indictment Was Returned (Dalton, Bartholomew). (Entered: 10/05/2023)\n\nResponse to Motion\n\n54\n\nOct 6, 2023\n\nMOTION for Richard I. G. Jones, Jr. to Withdraw as Attorney by Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Jones, Richard) (Entered: 10/06/2023)\n\nMotion to Withdraw as Attorney\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n55\n\nOct 11, 2023\n\nORDER granting 52 Amended Motion to Dismiss Felony Information as to Robert Hunter Biden. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 10/11/2023. (as) (Entered: 10/11/2023)\n\nOrder on Motion to Dismiss\n\n56\n\nOct 13, 2023\n\nMOTION to Amend/Correct 48 Order to Continue - Pretrial Motion Filing by Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Dalton, Bartholomew) (Entered: 10/13/2023)\n\nMotion to Amend/Correct\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n57\n\nOct 19, 2023\n\nORDER as to Robert Hunter Biden GRANTING 56 MOTION to Amend/Correct 48 Order to Continue - Pretrial Motion Filing. Pretrial Motions due by 12/11/2023; Government's responses due by 1/16/2024; and Defendant's replies due by 1/30/2024. Time is excluded from 10/19/2023 until 12/11/2023. Signed by Judge Maryellen Noreika on 10/19/2023. (as) (Entered: 10/19/2023)\n\nOrder\n\n58\n\nNov 15, 2023\n\nMOTION for Issuance of Rule 17(c) Subpoenas and Memorandum In Support by Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Subpoena to Donald John Trump, # 2 Subpoena to Jeffrey A Rosen, # 3 Subpoena to Richard Donoghue, # 4 Subpoena to William Barr)(Dalton, Bartholomew) (Entered: 11/15/2023)\n\nMotion for Miscellaneous Relief\n\nSubpoena to Donald John Trump\n\nSubpoena to Jeffrey A Rosen\n\nSubpoena to Richard Donoghue\n\nSubpoena to William Barr\n\n59\n\nDec 4, 2023\n\nRESPONSE to Motion by USA as to Robert Hunter Biden re 58 MOTION for Issuance of Rule 17(c) Subpoenas and Memorandum In Support (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Hines, Derek) (Entered: 12/04/2023)\n\nResponse to Motion\n\nText of Proposed Order\n\n60\n\nDec 11, 2023\n\nMOTION to Dismiss the Indictment Based on Immunity Conferred by his Diversion Agreement by Robert Hunter Biden. (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit 1 Executed Diversion Agreement, # 2 Exhibit 2 Declaration of Christopher J. Clark (with Exhibits), # 3 Exhibit A, # 4 Exhibit B, # 5 Exhibit C, # 6 Exhibit D, # 7 Exhibit E, # 8 Exhibit F, # 9 Exhibit G, # 10 Exhibit H, # 11 Exhibit I, # 12 Exhibit J, # 13 Exhibit K, # 14 Exhibit L, # 15 Exhibit M, # 16 Exhibit N, # 17 Exhibit O, # 18 Exhibit P, # 19 Exhibit Q, # 20 Exhibit R, # 21 Exhibit S, # 22 Exhibit T, # 23 Exhibit 3 Hunter Bidens Pretrial Diversion Report, dated July